---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="SoundThinking / ShotSpotter | Providers | NoRec.US" description="Acoustic gunshot-detection and public-safety technology; formerly known corporately as ShotSpotter." active="surveillance">
<main class="page_shell provider_detail">
  <header class="article_header provider_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">PROVIDER / PLATFORM</p>
    <h1>SoundThinking / ShotSpotter</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">Acoustic gunshot-detection and public-safety technology; formerly known corporately as ShotSpotter.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="provider_scope_notice">
    <span class="status_label">EVIDENCE SCOPE</span>
    <p><strong>Vendor capability</strong> describes the provider’s published product features. <strong>Illinois deployment</strong> is listed only when supported by Illinois records or a clearly labeled secondary source.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLINOIS CONNECTION</p>
    <h2>Documented Illinois relationships</h2>
    <div class="provider_evidence_grid">
      <article><span class="status_label">HISTORICALLY DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Chicago Police Department</h3><p>Chicago contracted for an area acoustic gunshot-surveillance system and the Chicago OIG published a detailed analysis of CPD's use. Chicago ended the deployment in 2024.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED PROCUREMENT</span><h3>Illinois State Police</h3><p>Illinois procurement records document ShotSpotter technology for Chicago expressway gunshot detection.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">VENDOR IDENTITY</span><h3>SoundThinking</h3><p>The company announced in 2023 that ShotSpotter, the company, would operate under the SoundThinking name while ShotSpotter remained a product/technology brand.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT / PLATFORM CAPABILITY</p>
    <h2>Published product capabilities</h2>
    <div class="provider_capability_grid">
      <article><h3>ShotSpotter</h3><p>Acoustic sensors and software detect impulsive sounds, estimate likely gunfire locations, and send alerts for human review and response.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Acoustic network</h3><p>The system's surveillance footprint depends on sensor placement and contracted coverage area.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Other SoundThinking products</h3><p>SoundThinking markets additional public-safety technologies. Their existence does not establish Illinois use.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / GOVERNANCE QUESTIONS</p>
    <h2>Privacy and governance</h2>
    <div class="provider_questions">
      <details><summary>Historical/current status matters</summary><p>Chicago's CPD deployment is labeled historically confirmed because the relationship ended in 2024.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Performance and outcomes</summary><p>Vendor claims, agency outcome claims and independent/OIG analysis should be presented separately.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Sensor scope</summary><p>A contract for acoustic gunshot detection does not establish unrelated audio surveillance capabilities.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="official_product_links">
    <p class="eyebrow">OFFICIAL PRODUCT INFORMATION</p>
    <h2>Vendor documentation</h2>
    <p>Vendor pages describe current products and features. Illinois deployment claims remain tied to Illinois-specific evidence.</p>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://www.soundthinking.com/" rel="external">SoundThinking product information</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.soundthinking.com/blog/shotspotter-is-now-soundthinking/" rel="external">ShotSpotter / SoundThinking company history</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE REFERENCES</p>
    <h2>Illinois records and supporting sources</h2>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://webapps1.chicago.gov/vcsearch/city/contracts/71366">City of Chicago Contract 71366 — ShotSpotter</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.oversight.gov/reports/chicago-police-departments-use-shotspotter-technology">Chicago OIG — CPD use of ShotSpotter</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.bidbuy.illinois.gov/bso/external/bidDetail.sda?docId=22-493ISP-OPERA-B-29936&external=true&parentUrl=close">Illinois BidBuy — ISP ShotSpotter procurement</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="hero_actions">
    <a class="button button_dark" href="/surveillance/">Back to Surveillance</a>
